The atomic category phrase selection in worker.py is adapted from
GroundingDINO groundingdino/util/inference.py (predict, remove_combined=True),
IDEA-Research, commit 856dde20aee659246248e20734ef9ba5214f5e44.
Source: https://github.com/IDEA-Research/GroundingDINO
Licensed under Apache License 2.0; see GroundingDINO-LICENSE.

The adaptation uses the installed Hugging Face tokenizer, retains the existing
box thresholds and NMS, and confines atomic phrase selection to source category
classification. Scene object and limb detection keep their native labels.

Unclassified proposals are discarded before non-maximum suppression. No class is
inferred for an empty phrase; preparation still rejects an unsupported source
category or an ambiguous scene placement.
